  "summary": "rrs 0.4.106 covertly exfiltrates screenshots and host identifiers to a hardcoded Discord webhook on CLI launch",
  "details": "The package advertises itself as an 'RRS P2P Network' chat tool but on invocation of its `rrs` console script, `rrs/__main__.py` spawns a daemon thread that runs `run_capture()` from `rrs/capture.py`, wrapped in a bare `try/except: pass` so any failure is silently swallowed. `run_capture()` uses `mss` to grab the primary monitor via `sct.grab(sct.monitors[0])` and POSTs the resulting PNG together with the hostname and username to a hardcoded Discord webhook at `https://discord.com/api/webhooks/1549807268294303860/...`. This screenshot-and-host-identity exfiltration is undisclosed, unrelated to the advertised P2P chat purpose, has no user prompt or opt-in, and delivers installer-side data to an attacker-controlled destination.",
